# A bare `return` at the opening level closes a sub (P0, author 2026-09-24): the body of s ends
# there, and each call runs it -- s prints `s 3` twice.  (The bare return used to stay an item of the
# unit, which the translator refused as "unsupported body".)  The unit's y stays 0: this is the
# author's example of Q52 (2026-09-28) -- «это независимое действие»: y is s's hidden input, and
# `y: y + 3` changes only that value of s's activation.  Entry 0.
int: y 0

sub: s ()
    y: y + 3
    c.printf: "s %d\n" y
return

s()
s
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: y; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
